description:
## Objective
Create delete mutations that E2E test cleanup requires.

## Problem
ConvexTestClient calls these mutations in cleanup(), but they don't exist:
- `api.tradingPartners.deletePartner`
- `api.transactions.deleteTransaction`

Tests will crash on cleanup without these.

## Implementation

### tradingPartners.ts
```typescript
export const deletePartner = mutation({
  args: { id: v.id('tradingPartners') },
  handler: async (ctx, args) => {
    const identity = await ctx.auth.getUserIdentity()
    if (!identity) throw new ConvexError('Authentication required')
    await ctx.db.delete(args.id)
  },
})
```

### transactions.ts
```typescript
export const deleteTransaction = mutation({
  args: { id: v.id('transactions') },
  handler: async (ctx, args) => {
    const identity = await ctx.auth.getUserIdentity()
    if (!identity) throw new ConvexError('Authentication required')
    await ctx.db.delete(args.id)
  },
})
```

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] `deletePartner` mutation exists and works
- [ ] `deleteTransaction` mutation exists and works
- [ ] Both require authentication
- [ ] E2E cleanup no longer crashes
